module gunbc.interpreter_replacement_cut

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr, Bool, List }
import gunbc.replacement_cut {
  ReplacementCutId,
  CoverageOpen,
  ConsumerDisposition, RetainSameContract, ReplacedByY, EvidenceOnly, Retire, Undecided,
  BoundaryConsumer,
  BoundaryCensus, ConsumersEnumerated,
  HigherBoundaryAnswer, DescentParentUnauthored,
  EvidenceDisposition, ReenrollAgainstY, RetireEvidence,
  ExternalXAnswer, ExternalXRoles, ExternalDifferentialOracle, HistoricalMeasurementSource,
  ReplacementCut,
  PlanAdmission,
  admit_replacement_cut_plan,
}

data interpreter_replacement_cut_note: String = "THE FIRST PRODUCTION ReplacementCut IN THE REPOSITORY. X is the v1 tree-walking interpreter; Y is native execution of the same .dag subjects. The row is authored from a measured deletion rather than from imagination: the deletion was performed on integration/interpreter-cut and the boundary population read from the far side of it, which is the only side it is visible from.\n\nWHY THIS PLAN REFUSES, and why the refusal is the deliverable: admit_replacement_cut_plan returns PlanRefused with counted causes, and every cause is a TRUE open decision rather than an authoring defect. Two classes. UNDECIDED: the driver region is another lane's boundary and the cut above it is unauthored, so no disposition can be earned here. UNCOVERED SURVIVING: the consumers that must keep working have no coverage authority to name, because the routing roster that would execute what X executes declares its own landing state as all-interpreted with the native flip LAST -- 77 ReadsLiveTree plus 35 host-effect entries ceilinged into a lane that does not exist. Naming a coverage authority anyway would be the fallback-wearing-a-disposition move the carrier already refuses; naming Y as covering a consumer Y does not cover is the same lie one level up. So the plan is authored to refuse and the causes are counted.\n\nWHAT THE COUNT IS, STATED AT ITS REAL SCOPE (corrected after review): the causes are the known unresolved dispositions AMONG THE SAMPLED CONSUMERS, UNDER ONE CANDIDATE Y. They are not a complete consumer census, not a semantic-feature census, and not a work estimate. An earlier revision of this note called them the honest size of what remains, which is an overclaim on two axes at once: the census enumerates ten of 125 files by its own declaration, and the refusal is evaluated against native execution alone.\n\nAND WHAT THE REFUSAL DOES NOT ESTABLISH: new_root names native execution through emitted Rust, so this plan's refusal shows that THAT realization does not presently cover the retained consumers. It does not show that no realization could. Any other candidate -- a fresh, smaller, fail-closed evaluator among them -- is excluded here BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by evidence, and no such candidate has been built, run, or refused. The choice of native execution is a received direction, not a conclusion derived in this carrier; a row that states a received constraint without saying so is indistinguishable from a row that concluded it. CORRECTED: new_root now names the boundary in CONSUMER terms and no longer in one realization's vocabulary. The two are different decisions and only the second is fixed by direction. Section 3 is explicit that the interface shape is what is owned, that a transport is one of N and never a fact about the dependency, and that the dispatch selecting a realization is itself realization and sits peripheral rather than in the interface. A replacement contract naming emitted Rust fused those, which is the mechanical reason every reading of this plan terminated at the native routing roster: that measures ONE REALIZATION'S COVERAGE and it is not the contract's denominator. The contract's denominator is reachable expression forms, reachable primitive identities, required effect kinds and required result shapes.\n\nTHE SELECTED REALIZATION, named where it belongs and cited rather than asserted: native execution through emitted Rust is the realization chosen behind this boundary, by operator direction. It is a received choice, not a conclusion derived in this carrier, and it is recorded as a selection so that it cannot be mistaken for a property of the contract. Restating it in new_root is what made this plan unable to express any other candidate. Whether an additional realization may be EVALUATED against this same boundary is an open question above this lane; the boundary's vocabulary does not decide it in either direction, which is precisely why the boundary is stated this way.\n\nA CONSEQUENCE WORTH CARRYING: on a boundary stated in consumer terms, cli_run is a CONSUMER of DagExecution and not automatically the parent cut. The unauthored-parent finding recorded in why_not_higher may therefore be an artifact of drawing the boundary at a FILE rather than at a contract, in which case it dissolves rather than needing to be solved. That arm is left as authored until it is re-measured at this boundary, because replacing a measured finding with a predicted one is the same error in the other direction.\n\nCENSUS GRAIN, declared: one row per distinct consuming module or binary, selected as the measured top of the reference distribution on main at 7f5fa6a94ec1 (1350 line-hits across 125 files; the ten rows below carry 1004 of them). This is NOT proven equal to the real boundary population -- the carrier states that limitation for every plan, and it holds here: an omitted consumer cannot be detected at this grain. The remaining 115 files are the residue this row does not enumerate, and that residue is a known omission rather than a claim of completeness.\n\nWHAT THAT REFERENCE COUNT DOES AND DOES NOT MEASURE: it measures ENTANGLEMENT -- how much code reaches X -- and it does not measure surviving OBLIGATIONS. Reliance establishes migration cost, never correctness, so the line-hit total is a selection instrument for census grain and nothing else. It must not be quoted as the size of the cut: the number that would be is how many of those references survive dispositioning, and that is not knowable until the boundary is settled.\n\nCORRECTION (row disposition, found by review after landing): coproduct_reflection and pre_push were authored Undecided on the stated ground that no disposition could be earned at an unauthored parent boundary. The measured branch DELETES both files, so this carrier reported an open decision for two consumers the artifact had already disposed of -- a false statement in a landed plan that other lanes read. Both are now Retire, because the deletion IS the disposition. cli_run remains Undecided and that is not the same defect: its region belongs to another lane, and parking a decision that is genuinely not this lane's to make is the honest arm rather than an error. Recorded here rather than silently amended, because a plan that corrects itself without saying so is indistinguishable from one that was always right.\n\nAND A DISPUTE THAT RIDES ON THOSE TWO ROWS, recorded because ratifying it silently would be the worse error: Retire here reports WHAT THE MEASURED BRANCH DID, not that deleting those consumers was methodologically sound. Review has since held that deleting consumers and behavioral sensors alongside X damages the experiment -- once a demand signal is removed, the absence of further failure no longer means the behavior was not load-bearing, it may only mean nothing is left to ask. A consumer earns Retire by being dispositioned, not by having been deleted. These two rows are therefore accurate as a record of the branch and are NOT a finding that the behavior had no surviving subject."

data interpreter_cut_identity: ReplacementCutId = "cut-v1-interpreter" as ReplacementCutId

fn nes(s: String) -> NonEmptyStr { s as NonEmptyStr }

fn consumer(name: String, disposition: ConsumerDisposition) -> BoundaryConsumer {
  BoundaryConsumer { consumer: nes(s: name), disposition: disposition }
}

// Retired: every row whose ONLY subject is X itself. These are not losses --
// their subject leaves with X, so retaining them would be retaining a claim
// about a thing that no longer exists.
fn retired_with_x() -> List<BoundaryConsumer> {
  [
    consumer(
      name: "gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface",
      disposition: Retire { reason: nes(s: "its entire subject is X's primitive dispatch arms") },
    ),
    consumer(
      name: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated",
      disposition: Retire { reason: nes(s: "generated projection of X's dispatch table; no authority survives it") },
    ),
    consumer(
      name: "gunbc.v1_interpreter_dispatch_emit",
      disposition: Retire { reason: nes(s: "the emitter whose only output is X's dispatch table") },
    ),
  ]
}

// Retired for a DIFFERENT reason, and kept in their own bucket because of it:
// these are not rows whose subject is X. They are consumers the measured branch
// deleted outright. Folding them in above would have let one bucket comment
// describe two classes -- a description that no longer matches its contents is
// the same stale-claim defect this carrier was just corrected for.
fn retired_by_deletion_on_the_measured_branch() -> List<BoundaryConsumer> {
  [
    consumer(
      name: "v1_compiler.coproduct_reflection",
      disposition: Retire { reason: nes(s: "deleted by the measured cut; the deletion is the disposition, not a finding that the behavior had no surviving subject") },
    ),
    consumer(
      name: "v1_compiler.pre_push",
      disposition: Retire { reason: nes(s: "deleted by the measured cut; the deletion is the disposition, not a finding that the behavior had no surviving subject") },
    ),
  ]
}

// Undecided, and honestly so: the driver region belongs to another lane's
// boundary, and the cut above BOTH lanes has not been authored. A disposition
// here would be authored by the wrong lane at the wrong boundary.
//
// CORRECTED: this arm previously also carried coproduct_reflection and pre_push
// as Undecided. The measured branch DELETES both files, so the row reported an
// open decision for two consumers the artifact had already disposed of -- a
// false statement in a landed carrier that other lanes read. The deletion IS
// the disposition; both moved to Retire below. cli_run stays here because its
// region genuinely belongs to another lane and parking it is not an error.
fn undecided_at_the_parent_boundary() -> List<BoundaryConsumer> {
  [
    consumer(name: "v1_compiler.cli_run", disposition: Undecided),
  ]
}

// Surviving with no coverage authority to name. Y does not cover them today and
// saying otherwise is the whole class this carrier exists to refuse.
fn surviving_without_coverage() -> List<BoundaryConsumer> {
  [
    consumer(
      name: "v1_compiler.bin.claim_executor",
      disposition: RetainSameContract {
        justification: nes(s: "the floor executor must keep executing every enrolled witness"),
        coverage: CoverageOpen,
      },
    ),
    consumer(
      name: "v1_compiler.bin.interp_recorded_fixture_witness",
      disposition: RetainSameContract {
        justification: nes(s: "recorded-fixture replay has no native route"),
        coverage: CoverageOpen,
      },
    ),
    consumer(
      name: "v1_compiler.bin.auth_declared_but_unwired_witness",
      disposition: RetainSameContract {
        justification: nes(s: "probe binary still reached through X's evaluation entry"),
        coverage: CoverageOpen,
      },
    ),
  ]
}

// Already carried by an authority that is not X: the primitive identity join was
// re-grounded on its four surviving surfaces when X's roster left.
fn regrounded_on_y() -> List<BoundaryConsumer> {
  [
    consumer(
      name: "std.primitive_identity",
      disposition: ReplacedByY { new_authority: nes(s: "std.primitive_identity four-surface derived census") },
    ),
  ]
}

fn interpreter_cut_consumers() -> List<BoundaryConsumer> {
  concat(
    concat(retired_with_x(), retired_by_deletion_on_the_measured_branch()),
    concat(
      concat(undecided_at_the_parent_boundary(), surviving_without_coverage()),
      regrounded_on_y(),
    ),
  )
}

fn interpreter_cut_region() -> List<NonEmptyStr> {
  [
    nes(s: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter"),
    nes(s: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated"),
    nes(s: "gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface"),
    nes(s: "gunbc.v1_interpreter_dispatch_emit"),
  ]
}

// X's permitted external roles. The standing operator grant is compile-checking
// only: a main-built binary containing X may typecheck sources on a branch that
// has deleted X. It is never a fallback, never an internal resolver, never a
// production second opinion -- and none of those has a constructor here, which
// is what makes the grant structural rather than remembered.
fn interpreter_cut_external_x() -> ExternalXAnswer {
  ExternalXRoles { roles: [ExternalDifferentialOracle, HistoricalMeasurementSource] }
}

fn interpreter_cut_evidence() -> List<EvidenceDisposition> {
  [
    ReenrollAgainstY {
      evidence: nes(s: "cross_representation_equality guard witness"),
      surviving_claim: nes(s: "a cross-representation equality straddle refuses rather than answering false"),
    },
    RetireEvidence {
      evidence: nes(s: "interpreter_dispatch_bijection_real_roster_red"),
      retired_subject: nes(s: "bijection between X's dispatch arms and its declared roster"),
      retirement_reason: nes(s: "the bijection's two sides both leave with X") ,
    },
  ]
}

fn interpreter_cut_why_not_higher() -> HigherBoundaryAnswer {
  DescentParentUnauthored {
    intended_parent_boundary: nes(s: "the engine cut through the v1 driver region"),
    basis: nes(s: "no cut is authored at that boundary by any lane: the cli_run lane's ruled scope is the driver verbs and it places this region explicitly outside its own, so both lanes descend from one unauthored parent"),
  }
}

fn interpreter_replacement_cut() -> ReplacementCut {
  ReplacementCut {
    identity: interpreter_cut_identity,
    old_root_consumer: nes(s: "v1 .dag evaluation entry"),
    subject: nes(s: "every .dag subject executed by the v1 tree-walking interpreter: enrolled witnesses, plan evaluation, and lens execution"),
    contract: nes(s: "evaluate a resolved .dag declaration to a value, or refuse with a typed located diagnostic; no fabricated plausible output"),
    new_root: nes(s: "the DagExecution boundary: evaluate(resolved_graph, entry, arguments, execution_mode, capabilities) -> Value | LocatedDiagnostic | UnsupportedFeature"),
    why_not_higher: interpreter_cut_why_not_higher(),
    covered_region: interpreter_cut_region(),
    boundary_census: ConsumersEnumerated { consumers: interpreter_cut_consumers() },
    external_x: interpreter_cut_external_x(),
    evidence_dispositions: interpreter_cut_evidence(),
  }
}

fn interpreter_cut_admission() -> PlanAdmission {
  admit_replacement_cut_plan(cut: interpreter_replacement_cut())
}
